# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# os
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.log

# probe output IS committed. Every determinism and stability number in eval/REPORT.md and
# probes/RESULTS.md is derived from these files, and a number nobody can check is just a claim.
# `npm run evidence` recomputes the headline figures straight from them.
# (Checked for credentials before un-ignoring: they hold distributions, verdicts and token
#  counts, no keys and no Authorization headers.)

# graphify working files (graph.json + report are kept)
graphify-out/.graphify_*
graphify-out/cache/

# their cloned exercise repo — read-only, never modified, never committed.
# If the eval harness needs the fixtures, we make our OWN copy elsewhere.
exercise-source/

# supabase CLI scratch
supabase/.temp/

# compilation intermediates — regenerate via scripts/assemble-packs.mjs
.scratch/

# Scorer output IS committed. These are the runs eval/REPORT.md quotes — including
# coaching-01.run1.json, which is the second determinism run and the only way anyone can verify
# the "11 of 12 identical" claim rather than taking it on trust.
eval/out/*
!eval/out/*.json

# report page backups from local edit sessions — regenerate with `npm run render`
app/index.bak*.html
.vercel
.scratch/

# ids of the demo runs seeded by `npm run browser-seed` — machine-local, regenerate
test/browser/seeded.json

# Process artefacts, kept locally and not published. Superseded by app/index.html (the deck the
# app actually serves) and screenshots/ (what it looks like); none of it is referenced by any code.
wireframes/
screens/
graphify-out/
research/
design/reference-frames/

# Working notes for the agent building this, and a backend scratch doc. Neither is a deliverable.
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF-BACKEND.md
